              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux versions through 2.41.5 and 2.42.2 fail to check mount helper exit status before running post-mount hooks, allowing unprivileged users to execute privileged operations on pre-existing filesystems. Attackers can exploit X-mount.idmap or X-mount.owner hooks to clone filesystems with inherited suid bits or modify target inode permissions after a helper fails, achieving privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-76642",
              "help": {
